  "title": "Cedar Garden Gate",
  "summary": "A 36 in wide braced cedar gate on a wood H-frame that stays square in wet weather.",
  "difficulty": "intermediate",
  "estimatedHours": 5,
  "imageUrl": null,
  "currency": "USD",
  "steps": [
    "Cut the two rails and three uprights from cedar, then lay them on a flat surface and clamp.",
    "Set the diagonal brace from the bottom hinge corner to the top latch corner so the gate self-squares.",
    "Screw the brace into the uprights with wide-face screws, then screw the rails to the uprights.",
    "Cut the two posts, set them plumb in concrete, and check the gate opening is square.",
    "Hang the gate on heavy galvanised hinges and fit a drop rod so the latch is not the only keeper.",
    "Sand and apply two coats of exterior sealer."
  ],
